{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1205 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "ae80867f79a341eaba5548fe124babf0328c37837a41cf0a3cfdcbf304bd7cc1" :edb/db-before-t 1204 :edb/db-after-t 1205 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534517 50 #inst "2026-10-07T19:45:28.223Z" 13194139534517 true] [17592186059732 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292873 13194139534517 true] [17592186059775 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292829 13194139534517 true] [17592186078542 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292822 13194139534517 true] [17592186083210 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292857 13194139534517 true] [17592186092165 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292843 13194139534517 true] [17592186096548 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292863 13194139534517 true] [17592186110487 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292866 13194139534517 true] [17592186152162 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292836 13194139534517 true] [17592186212940 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292850 13194139534517 true] [17592186292822 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292823 13194139534517 true] [17592186292822 1089 "q-106832" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292822 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534517 true] [17592186292822 1100 "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2x-{x}^{3}}.$" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292822 1113 #uuid "d9250d96-2930-55be-a93d-b3b19673faf9" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292822 1145 "First, we rewrite the limit as\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2x-{x}^{3}}={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{3}-2x}.\n$$\n\nThe numerator here is a bounded, oscillating function with\n\n$$\n|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|\\le 1.\n$$\n\nHowever, the denominator ${x}^{3}-2x$ grows without bound as $x\\to \\infty .$ So the denominator is growing much faster than the numerator, and we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2x-{x}^{3}}={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{3}-2x}=0.\n$$\n\nWe can see this from the graph of $y=\\frac{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2x-{x}^{3}},$ shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/assets/a9d96a5a85181cddc6eb1bd5f79d6a0238ef16f060ddebf2dc4c48ef1911604f.png)" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292823 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292824 13194139534517 true] [17592186292823 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292825 13194139534517 true] [17592186292823 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292826 13194139534517 true] [17592186292823 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292827 13194139534517 true] [17592186292823 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292828 13194139534517 true] [17592186292823 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534517 true] [17592186292823 1041 "selection" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292823 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292827 13194139534517 true] [17592186292823 1110 #uuid "e3208868-49e5-557c-b01c-a936ff6cb30c" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292824 1034 "\\infty " 13194139534517 true] [17592186292824 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292824 1111 #uuid "5558984e-05d9-5ba1-9de2-fa71a77b8cf3" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292825 1034 "1" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292825 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292825 1111 #uuid "460ae15b-f4be-5514-98b7-e705956a073c" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292826 1034 "\\text{DNE}" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292826 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292826 1111 #uuid "9a6443fa-1a0b-51ee-b860-501184545d20" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292827 1034 "0" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292827 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292827 1111 #uuid "2946a868-1500-5d7a-8bff-44dd42e5e7d5" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292828 1034 "-2" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292828 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292828 1111 #uuid "39bbe88a-2431-597a-a713-28a16abe634b" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292829 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292830 13194139534517 true] [17592186292829 1089 "q-127838" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292829 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534517 true] [17592186292829 1100 "The vector $u$ has magnitude $6$, the vector $v$ has magnitude $4$, the angle between $u$ and $v$ is ${30}^{∘}$ and $n$ is the unit vector that points in the direction of $u\\times v.$ Find $u\\times v$ in terms of $n.$" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292829 1113 #uuid "6031cc66-ec95-5415-9785-9f9e09ec2735" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292829 1145 "We use the formula for the cross product and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|u|\\cdot |v|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =6\\cdot 4\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\  & =24\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot n \\\\  & =12n.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292830 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292831 13194139534517 true] [17592186292830 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292832 13194139534517 true] [17592186292830 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292833 13194139534517 true] [17592186292830 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292834 13194139534517 true] [17592186292830 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292835 13194139534517 true] [17592186292830 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534517 true] [17592186292830 1041 "selection" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292830 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292831 13194139534517 true] [17592186292830 1110 #uuid "5ba727a4-81fb-5a56-abce-ea644f58432e" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292831 1034 "12n" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292831 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292831 1111 #uuid "653644b0-5342-5dd7-ba29-a7cfaeade2ce" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292832 1034 "4n" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292832 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292832 1111 #uuid "c1cb6b65-0f97-5d5f-8b22-b8890e6797d7" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292833 1034 "18n" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292833 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292833 1111 #uuid "edaaac1a-88e2-518e-833f-77dc5e09265d" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292834 1034 "6n" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292834 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292834 1111 #uuid "137c510c-446c-5ac4-9206-222c6493612a" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292835 1034 "24n" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292835 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292835 1111 #uuid "a9f8ed7d-5bf0-5dcc-b9b7-d27afae13f7a" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292836 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292837 13194139534517 true] [17592186292836 1089 "q-134016" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292836 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534517 true] [17592186292836 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/assets/e2d51071ddc198adecdff56593dec29ba9aef10d90b89ddc03a4cdbe9c757034.png)\n\nWhat is the slope of the trend line shown above?" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292836 1113 #uuid "0a2a1e0f-109b-5eb1-aede-0460221885ac" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292836 1145 "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(0,8)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(3,7).$\n\nTherefore, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7-8}{3-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292837 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292838 13194139534517 true] [17592186292837 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292839 13194139534517 true] [17592186292837 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292840 13194139534517 true] [17592186292837 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292841 13194139534517 true] [17592186292837 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292842 13194139534517 true] [17592186292837 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534517 true] [17592186292837 1041 "selection" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292837 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292840 13194139534517 true] [17592186292837 1110 #uuid "de8facb1-7b54-5d95-8b90-671f98bba8ce" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292838 1034 "-\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292838 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292838 1111 #uuid "de8710da-d1c1-520a-ac96-3582c83f6d7a" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292839 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292839 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292839 1111 #uuid "994e93e7-c00a-5742-8a68-75269590ca63" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292840 1034 "-\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292840 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292840 1111 #uuid "d43841e2-859c-5834-b8b9-9fc0694c41b7" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292841 1034 "-\\frac{2}{7}" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292841 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292841 1111 #uuid "95660e11-a29a-5099-8d9d-0dc2000b2ab4" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292842 1034 "-\\frac{3}{7}" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292842 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292842 1111 #uuid "5158c879-7858-5855-87a8-1fd6c3fabb37" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292843 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292844 13194139534517 true] [17592186292843 1089 "q-17124" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292843 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534517 true] [17592186292843 1100 "Given that the distance from a point $P$ to the origin is $\\frac{1}{3},$ and that $P$ makes an angle of $\\frac{5\\pi }{4}$ with the positive $x$-axis, what are the Cartesian coordinates of $P?$" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292843 1113 #uuid "1600c079-8696-5fa4-9f4f-536830552848" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292843 1145 "We notice that the point $P$ is described using polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ where\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\theta =\\frac{5\\pi }{4}.\n$$\n\nTo convert from polar coordinates to Cartesian coordinates, we use\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the $x$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4}) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{-\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen we calculate the $y$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4}) \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{-\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $P$ are $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}).$" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292844 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292845 13194139534517 true] [17592186292844 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292846 13194139534517 true] [17592186292844 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292847 13194139534517 true] [17592186292844 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292848 13194139534517 true] [17592186292844 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292849 13194139534517 true] [17592186292844 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534517 true] [17592186292844 1041 "selection" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292844 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292847 13194139534517 true] [17592186292844 1110 #uuid "b636fb6d-c682-542b-b25c-749bd6dcf1f0" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292845 1034 "(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292845 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292845 1111 #uuid "0019a12c-e576-5a4b-b94b-3337d9bd793e" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292846 1034 "(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3})" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292846 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292846 1111 #uuid "b25b450c-fcf5-5490-96c8-5403facd11e4" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292847 1034 "(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6})" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292847 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292847 1111 #uuid "b0cbd1d3-638c-56ed-96b1-0b3edcc865f0" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292848 1034 "(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{5},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{5})" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292848 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292848 1111 #uuid "0d70bf82-a79c-5359-bc83-3c6414396490" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292849 1034 "(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4})" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292849 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292849 1111 #uuid "9b29f011-514a-5612-b515-2c1d43c38312" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292850 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292851 13194139534517 true] [17592186292850 1089 "q-288444" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292850 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534517 true] [17592186292850 1100 "The following equation is true for all values of $x.$\n\n$$\n-2{x}^{2}+3x+b=-2{x}^{2}+3x-6\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of the constant $b?$" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292850 1113 #uuid "f0b2734f-0ee6-5285-8bef-0e313bb618ab" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292850 1145 "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nWe compare the constant terms on both sides. On the left-hand side, the constant is $b.$ On the right-hand side, the constant is $-6.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nb=-6.\n$$" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292851 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292852 13194139534517 true] [17592186292851 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292853 13194139534517 true] [17592186292851 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292854 13194139534517 true] [17592186292851 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292855 13194139534517 true] [17592186292851 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292856 13194139534517 true] [17592186292851 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534517 true] [17592186292851 1041 "selection" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292851 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292856 13194139534517 true] [17592186292851 1110 #uuid "0931fc79-d008-5b67-8515-1a375ae7f283" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292852 1034 "3" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292852 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292852 1111 #uuid "4b720bf6-ab1f-5f5b-b28b-bd2d9226c53b" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292853 1034 "6" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292853 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292853 1111 #uuid "838eda95-a363-598c-b42f-c95bc7f93707" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292854 1034 "-3" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292854 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292854 1111 #uuid "d8b50d2d-73a8-50e5-be21-8640d6f0cf0a" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292855 1034 "0" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292855 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292855 1111 #uuid "0db79e22-5124-5430-8d80-42a1d499b503" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292856 1034 "-6" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292856 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292856 1111 #uuid "95698a32-4eb8-5163-b62c-1cbbf4c09e8f" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292857 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292858 13194139534517 true] [17592186292857 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292861 13194139534517 true] [17592186292857 1089 "q-328382" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292857 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534517 true] [17592186292857 1100 "The center of the hyperbola ${x}^{2}-9{y}^{2}-6x-36y=54$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292857 1113 #uuid "dd806166-c3df-538e-871b-d9477c5bfc0b" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292857 1145 "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-9{y}^{2}-6x-36y & =54 \\\\ {x}^{2}-6x-9{y}^{2}-36y & =54 \\\\ [{x}^{2}-6x]-9[{y}^{2}+4y] & =54 \\\\ [(x-3)^{2}-9]-9[(y+2)^{2}-4] & =54 \\\\ (x-3)^{2}-9-9(y+2)^{2}+36 & =54 \\\\ (x-3)^{2}-9(y+2)^{2} & =54+9-36 \\\\ (x-3)^{2}-9(y+2)^{2} & =27 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{27})^{2}}-\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{27})^{2}}-\\frac{(y-(-2))^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,3,-2\\,).$" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292858 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292859 13194139534517 true] [17592186292858 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292860 13194139534517 true] [17592186292858 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534517 true] [17592186292858 1041 "field-1" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292858 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292859 13194139534517 true] [17592186292858 1110 #uuid "ed6a1d8b-b783-5448-957c-feea21ab1621" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292859 1034 "3" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292859 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292859 1111 #uuid "b8e3be0f-25a5-51fe-a9ad-5cbaebe7ef10" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292860 1034 "-3" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292860 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292860 1111 #uuid "f1af8e26-b3f1-5767-9bbb-95792354f892" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292861 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292862 13194139534517 true] [17592186292861 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534517 true] [17592186292861 1041 "field-2" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292861 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292862 13194139534517 true] [17592186292861 1110 #uuid "4c460dcd-9be9-542b-8990-d412f56cf644" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292862 1034 "-2" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292862 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292862 1111 #uuid "24c5fd38-fad6-58fe-9efa-6cb6358a5d06" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292863 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292864 13194139534517 true] [17592186292863 1089 "q-351278" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292863 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534517 true] [17592186292863 1100 "Express $\\frac{9{x}^{2}-6x+20}{(2{x}^{2}+5)x}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{9{x}^{2}-6x+20}{(2{x}^{2}+5)x}=\\,$ | $x\\,-\\,${{field-1}} | $+$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $2{x}^{2}+5$ |  | $x$ |" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292863 1113 #uuid "55bbc0e5-8d38-5973-b1f1-afc64d12e238" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292863 1145 "Our task is to find $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9{x}^{2}-6x+20}{(2{x}^{2}+5)x}=\\frac{x+B}{2{x}^{2}+5}+\\frac{4}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(2{x}^{2}+5)x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}-6x+20 & =(x+B)x+4(2{x}^{2}+5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9(1)^{2}-6(1)+20 & =(1+B)(1)+4(2(1)^{2}+5) \\\\ 23 & =1+B+28 \\\\ B & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{9{x}^{2}-6x+20}{(2{x}^{2}+5)x}=\\frac{x-6}{2{x}^{2}+5}+\\frac{4}{x}\n$$" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292864 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292865 13194139534517 true] [17592186292864 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534517 true] [17592186292864 1041 "field-1" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292864 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292865 13194139534517 true] [17592186292864 1110 #uuid "c7354aa1-1525-55a5-8a28-58ba28267f4f" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292865 1034 "6" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292865 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534517 true] [17592186292865 1111 #uuid "b84caf6b-47a6-51dd-bc22-d93398b42e45" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292866 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292867 13194139534517 true] [17592186292866 1089 "q-65463" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292866 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534517 true] [17592186292866 1100 "Simplify $\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-1}-1.$" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292866 1113 #uuid "e148983a-5035-5901-aa4f-54a3e738d0a1" 13194139534517 true] [17592186292866 1145 "First, we multiply the numerator and the denominator of the fraction by $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+1.$ This gives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-1} & =\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-1}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x\\,(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+1)}{{csc}^{2}⁡x-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the identity ${csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -1={cot}^{2}⁡\\theta $, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x\\,(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+1)}{{csc}^{2}⁡x-1}-1 & =\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x\\,(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+1)}{{cot}^{2}⁡x}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{cot}^{2}⁡x}\\,(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+1)}{\\cancel{{cot}^{2}⁡x}}-1 \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+1)\\,-1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}